_pdbx_entry_details.sequence_details         
;hMPV F is a class I fusion glycoprotein, synthesized as an inactive precursor (F0) that needs to be cleaved to become fusion competent. Proteolytic cleavage generates two disulfide-linked subunits (F2 N-terminal and F1 C-terminal fragments) that assemble into a homotrimer. Specifically, REEQIENPRQSKKRKRR at the C-terminus of Fusion glycoprotein F2 is cleaved after trypsin treatment. VATAAAVTAGIAIAKTIR at the N-terminus of Fusion glycoprotein F1 and KGNTSGRENLYFQGGGGGSGYIPEAPRDQAYVRKDGEWVLLSTFLGGTEGR at the C-terminus of Fusion glycoprotein F1 are cleaved after trypsin treatment.
